# EverShelf — Cline working rules

Self-hosted **pantry manager**: PHP 8 + SQLite backend, vanilla-JS SPA/PWA.
No framework, no runtime build step. Repo root = `/var/www/html/dispensa`.

**Read `AGENTS.md` first** — it is the full working guide. This file is the short
digest that always applies. Deep architecture: `docs/CODEBASE-MAP.md`.

**Roadmap & community**: `docs/ROADMAP.md` is the product-facing plan (what is next, the
effort involved, which issues are up for grabs; the pinned issue #290 is the community
entry point). New feature work: a roadmap entry + an issue, never a code-only change.
**Advertising is parked**: the banner slots are commented out and must stay that way —
read `docs/wiki/Support-and-ads.md` before touching `SUPPORT_*` / `ADS_*`.

## 1. Never read the giant files in full

| File | Size | How to navigate |
|---|---|---|
| `assets/js/app.js` | ~29 200 lines | `docs/INDEX-app-js.md` (function → line), then a ranged read |
| `api/index.php` | ~20 600 lines | `docs/INDEX-api-index.md` |
| `index.html` | ~2 770 lines | `grep -n` for the id you need |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | ~2 280 lines | never read whole; `head` it or anchor an edit on the top heading |
| `translations/*.json` | ~130 KB each | `python3 -c` + `grep` on the key, not the whole file |

Always locate with `grep -n "functionName" file` or the indexes, then read only
that range (`start_line`/`end_line`). `.clineignore` hides generated/vendor/
runtime/binary files — if a task truly needs one, ask first.

## 2. Conventions

- **Language**: code, comments and docs in **English**. UI strings must never be
  hardcoded: `t('key')` in JS / `data-i18n="key"` in HTML, and the key must be
  added to **all six** locales (it, en, de, fr, es, zh). Optional UI text coming
  from PHP returns a `hint_key` (+ `hint_args`) / `tip_key` / `reasons[]`, never a
  literal string.
- **Backend**: every HTTP action is one `case` in `switch ($action)` in
  `api/index.php` (+ its handler function below). Errors → `{"success":false,
  "error":"..."}` inside the existing global try/catch; never print HTML before
  JSON. Log with `EverLog::info/warn/error/debug/exception` and a
  `['event' => 'snake_case_key']` context — never `error_log`/`var_dump`.
- **Security**: new action → add it to the right allow-list in
  `api/lib/security.php` only when intended. Never trust client headers
  (`Origin`, `Referer`, `Sec-Fetch-Site`).
- **Frontend**: plain JS, `escapeHtml()` before any `innerHTML`; no inline
  `onclick` with unescaped data; use the `api(action, payload)` wrapper (app.js
  ~line 5384).
- **UI grammar**: one emerald (`--brand-primary`) per action strip for the action
  that writes the outcome, neutral secondaries for the rest, no pastel per-button
  colours; every banner action stays inline (never behind a ⋮). A product row opens
  with `_productThumbHtml()` (44×44, neutral frame, category emoji fallback — never
  a broken image or an empty square) — and a **medicine** opens with its own drawn
  mark (`_medIconMarkup()`, `assets/img/icons/medicine.svg`), never a food emoji:
  same for the plain emoji slots (`_productCatIconHtml()`), the `badge-medical`
  badge and the place icons (`_locIconMarkup()`), where the cabinet is the pill.
- **Product titles** (`products.name`/`kind`) go exclusively through
  `mergeIncomingProductFields()` in `api/index.php` + `api/lib/product_kind.php`.
  Never add a second dictionary or write a title elsewhere.
- **A title carries no HTML entities.** `productTitleDecodeEntities()` (inside
  `productTitleCapitalize()`, the one title choke point) decodes *repeatedly*
  (`&amp;quot;` → `&quot;` → `"`), the client's `decodeHtmlEntities()` does the same,
  and `migrateDB` repairs rows already stored escaped
  (`migration_decode_title_entities_v1`) — so neither the pantry, the history nor a
  toast can print `&quot;`.
- **Red is only for losing stock.** `_showDestructiveConfirm(title, msg, fn, label,
  { tone: 'positive' })` paints an emerald confirm and **no countdown** when the
  action puts stock back (undoing a consumption); red + countdown stays for
  throw / finish / take-stock-away.
- **SHELFY acts where the user stands.** A captured sentence never navigates to the
  legacy `#page-use`: `_shelfyRunConsume()` closes the sheet and shows the floating
  `.shelfy-confirm` card (avatar, “Registro {qty} di {name}”, a 10 s emerald bar
  draining right→left, Modifica / ✕ Annulla). The empty bar writes `inventory_use`;
  Modifica opens the compact product sheet (`showItemDetail(invId, productId, qty)`);
  “ho finito …” opens that same sheet with its slide-to-confirm. `_shelfyArmButton()`
  prints the remaining seconds in `.shelfy-arm-count`, so every countdown is visible.
- **SHELFY has a face**: `assets/img/shelfy/shelfy-avatar{,-192,-96}.png` (transparent
  PNG, in the `sw.js` shell) — the centre of the bottom nav, the capture sheet head,
  the intro hero and the confirm card. Never swap it for a food emoji.
- **Tablet/kiosk CSS is opt-in**: `assets/css/tablet.css` activates on `html.is-kiosk`
  / `html.is-touch-tablet` (set by `_markDeviceChrome()`), never on `min-width` alone —
  a desktop monitor keeps the base styles.
- **DB schema/migrations**: `api/database.php` (`initializeDB`, `migrateDB`).
- **Style**: follow the surrounding code, 4-space indent, docblock + comment
  style already in use; keep comments explanatory, not decorative.

## 3. Version / asset / i18n hygiene

- Version lives in **5 places** → always run `scripts/bump-version.sh X.Y.Z`
  (`index.html` badges, `manifest.json`, `sw.js` CACHE, `app.js` i18n token,
  `README.md` version badge), add a top `CHANGELOG.md` entry and prepend the
  release to the README “What’s new” line.
- Edited `app.js` / `style.css` → bump the `?v=` stamp in `index.html` and the
  `sw.js` CACHE name (the script above does it; the CACHE carries version + stamp
  letter and the stamp auto-increments within the same day).
- Entries with `t('key')` must be a literal, bare `t('…')` call — a helper or a
  PHP-only string is invisible to `scripts/i18n-audit.py`.

## 4. Validate before saying "done"

```bash
# syntax
find api -name '*.php' -exec php -l {} \;
node -c assets/js/app.js && node -c sw.js
for f in mcp-server/src/*.js; do node --check "$f"; done

# i18n
python3 -c "import json,glob; [json.load(open(f)) for f in glob.glob('translations/*.json')]"
python3 scripts/i18n-audit.py

# after big edits, regenerate the navigation indexes
bash scripts/gen-code-index.sh
```

Run locally: `php -S 127.0.0.1:8080` → http://127.0.0.1:8080

## 5. Git

- Work on **`develop`**; CI auto-merges `develop → main` and tags the release.
- Commit prefixes used in history: `feat:`, `fix:`, `release:`, `merge:`.
- Never commit `/todo/` (internal notes), `.env`, keystores or APKs.
- Don't touch `.github/workflows/*` pushes blindly: pushing workflow files needs
  a `workflow`-scoped PAT (see `todo/0001-ci-*.patch`).

## 6. Response style for this project

- Be concise: diff-first, no restating the whole file.
- State assumptions and any file you intentionally left out of scope.
- Report the exact commands you ran and their result.
